  <page>
    <title>List of characters from international versions of Sesame Street</title>
    <id>231437</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41498849</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-27T19:54:46Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>212.201.44.249</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* [[Susam Sokaği]] ([[Turkey]]) */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">''[[Sesame Street]]'' has many international versions across the world. Each uses some original characters, created specifically to represent their own culture. The following list highlights some of these characters. All characters are [[Muppets]], unless otherwise mentioned.

==[[Vila Sésamo]] ([[Brazil]])==
* Garibaldo, a giant, shy, blue bird. Similar to Big Bird.
* Gugu, a green Muppet monster with a blue nose and orange cheeks. Similar to Oscar the Grouch.
* Beto and Ênio, Bert and Ernie like characters.
* Juca (Armando Bogus), a toy maker who taught children his craft.
* Ana Maria (Sonia Braga), a teacher and Juca's cousin.
* Gabriela (Aracy Balabanian), wife of Juca
* Funga-funga, a red Muppet [[elephant]] who didn't like how others looked at him.

==[[Canada's Sesame Street]] and [[Sesame Park]] ([[Canada]])==
* [[Louis (Sesame Street)|Louis]], a French-Canadian otter
* [[Basil (Sesame Street)|Basil]], a polar bear
* [[Dodi (Sesame Street)|Dodi]], essentially a ''[[Jack-Of-All-Trades]]'', though most commonly known as a bush pilot.
* [[Katie]], a girl
* [[Chaos (Sesame Park character)|Chaos]], a cat
* [[Beau Beaver]], a beaver (animated)

==[[Zhima Jie]] ([[China]])==
* [[Da Niao]], similar to [[Big Bird]]
* [[Hu Hu Zhu]]
* [[Little Plum (Zhima Jie)|Little Plum]]

==[[Sesamstrasse]] ([[Germany]])==
* [[Samson (Sesamstrasse)|Samson]], a male bear, similar in role and full-body puppet, to Big Bird  (1978-present)
* [[Simson]], Samson's cousin and lookalike, often seen with a hat or a tie to distinguish him from Samson  (on and off in 1989-2000)
* [[Tiffy]], a pink female bird (1978-present)
* [[Finchen]], a (former male, now female) snail  (on and off from 1978, 1989-present)
* [[Rumpel]], an [[Oscar the Grouch]]-like male character that lives in a rainbarrel. He has [[Gustav (Sesamstraße)|Gustav]], a pet caterpillar (1989-present)
* [[Buh (Sesame Street character)|Buh]], a male owl (1989-present)
* [[Feli Filu]], a blue female monster reporter (2000-present)
* [[Pferd]], a male horse (2000-present)
* [[Wolle]], a male lamb (2000-present)
* [[Lena]], a pink monster baby (2005-present)
* [[Moni]], a female photographer (2005-present)

* [[Ulli von Bödefeld]], a male hedgehog-like creature (1978-early 1986)
* [[Leonie Löwenherz]], a lioness (1989-early 1990s)

===Humans in Sesamstrasse 1978-1986===
* Henning ([[Henning Venske]], a West German actor - 1978-1979)
* Lilo ([[Lieselotte Pulver]], a Swiss actress 1978-1986)
* Uwe ([[Uwe Friedrichsen]], a West German actor 1979-1982)
* Horst ([[Horst Janson]], a West German actor 1979-1986)
* Ute ([[Ute Willing]], a German actor 1979-1986)
* Ilse ([[Ilse Biberti]], a German actress 1979-1982)
* Elisabeth ([[Elisabeth Vitouch]], a German actress 1979-1982)
* Manfred ([[Manfred Krug]], an East German actor - 1982-1986)

===Humans in Sesamstrasse 1986-present===
* Georg ([[Gernot Endemann]], a German actor - 1986-1999)
* Bettina ([[Hildegard Krekel]], a German actress - 1986-1989)
* Bettina 2 ([[Kirsten Spick]], a German actress - 1989-1999)
* Opa Brass ([[Ferdinand Dux]], a German actor - 1992-2000)
* Pensionswirtin Helmi ([[Senta Bonneval]], a German actress - 1995-1999)
* Musiker Alex ([[Alexander Geringas]], a German-Greek actor - 1995-2000)
* Jiviana ([[Vijak Bajani]], a German-Turkish actress - 1995-2001)

* Nils ([[Nils Julius]], a German actor - 2000-present)
* Caro ([[Caroline Kiesewetter]], a German actress - 2000-2002)
* Caro 2 ([[Miriam Krause]], a German actress - 2002-present)
* Zauberer PePe ([[Dirk Bach]], a German comedian - 2000-present)
* Anke ([[Anke Engelke]], a German comedienne - 2003-present)
* Mehmet ([[Mehmet Yilmaz]], a German-Turkish actor - 2003-present)
* Ella ([[Franziska Troegner]], a German actress - 2003-present)

==[[Shalom Sesame]] ([[Israel]])==
* [[Kippi ben Kippod]], or Kippi Kippod, a giant [[porcupine]] analogous to [[Big Bird]]
* [[Moishe Oofnik]], [[Oscar the Grouch]]'s cousin grouch

==[[Iftah Ya Simsim]] ([[Kuwait]])==
* [[No'Man]], a camel equivlent of Big Bird
* [[Melsoon]], a light green parrot wearing a tie
* [[Yaqut]], a lavender monster with a long nose

==[[Plaza Sésamo]] ([[Mexico]])==
*[[Abelardo Montoya]], the equivalent of [[Big Bird]], with [[Green]] and [[Red]] feathers ([[Mexico]]'s [[National colours]]; also the colors of a [[Parrot]], one of [[Mexico]]'s most numerous and representative birds)
*[[Bodoque]], a [[grouch]] that lives in boxes
*[[Cuernos]] (Horns), a red monster with a characteristic couple of horns and vicious teeth.
*[[El Barón Púrpura]] (The Purple Baron), a Muppet portraying a lackluster air pilot. A satire of [[The Red Baron]].
*[[Lola (Plaza Sesamo)|Lola]], a female relative of [[Pancho]] and [[Abelardo]]'s best friend; a joyful young pink muppet.
*[[Paco (Plaza Sesamo)|Paco]], a [[parrot]], the equivalent of America's [[Oscar the Grouch]]
*[[Pancho]], a blue-colored [[monster]], who has a pet elephant [[Elefancio]], only the trunk is ever seen
*[[Multimonstruos]], Red Anything Monsters, appear as babies, pirates, etc.
*[[Multimuppets]], Brown Anything Muppets
*Four birds

==[[Sesamstraat]] ([[Netherlands]])==
* [[Pino]], a blue [[Big Bird]]-like character
* [[Tommie]], a dog
* [[Ieniemienie]], a mouse
* [[Purk]], a pig
* [[Troel]], Tommie's [[girlfriend]]

===Humans in Sesamstraat===
* [[Buurman Baasje]], male
* [[Elvan]], female
* [[Frank (Sesamstraat)|Frank]], male
* [[Gerda (Sesamstraat)|Gerda]], female
* [[Hakim (Sesamstraat)|Hakim]], male
* [[Lot (Sesamstraat)|Lot]], female
* [[Meneer Aart]], male
* [[Paula (Sesamstraat)|Paula]], female
* [[Rik (Sesamstraat)|Rik]], male
* [[Sien (Sesamstraat)|Sien]], female

==[[Sesam Stasjon]] ([[Norway]])==
* [[Max Mekker]]: a big blue monster who owns a train station called &quot;Sesam Stasjon&quot;.
* [[Alfa]]: a female yellow monster.
* [[Bjarne]]: a pink man who owns a ticket booth.

==[[Sesame!]] or [[Batibot]] ([[Philippines]])==
*[[Pong Pagong]], a clumsy, pink full-body turtle wearing a baseball cap.
*[[Kiko Matsing]], a purple gorilla version of Oscar.
*[[Koko Kwik-Kwak]] or [[Koko]], a four-year-old bird-child inspired by ''[[Pag-asa]]'', the first [[Philippine eagle]] hatched under laboratory conditions.
*[[Manang Bola]], the forgetful fortuneteller.
*[[Kapitan Basa]], a [[superhero]] that loves to read. 
*[[Sitsiritsit]] and [[Alibangbang]], two inquisitive [[space aliens]].
*[[Sultan Parachibum]], a ''[[datu]]'' or [[chieftain]] of ''[[Agamanyog]]'' whose official advisers are his granchildren. 
*[[Ningning]] and [[Gingging]], two sisters. ''Ningning'' is the eldest and a serious type, while ''Gingging'' is younger and playful.
*[[Noli de Kasyo]], the prolific journalist. 
*[[Irma Daldal]], a stage-struck, faddish, shallow and cheap actress who believes she is the most talented person in all of show business.  
*[[Direk]], a movie-and-television [[director]], who tries everything to make a star out of  the actress ''Irma Daldal''.

===Humans in Batibot===
*[[Kuya Bodjie]] (Brother Bodjie Pascual)
*[[Ate Sienna]] (Sister Sienna)

==[[Rua Sésamo]] ([[Portugal]])==
* [[Poupas]], an orange version of Big Bird.
* [[Ferrão]], brown-colored version of Oscar the Grouch that lived inside a bottomless barrel in the Sesame Street square.
* [[Tita]], a gray cat.

==[[Ulitsa Sezam]] ([[Russia]])==
* [[Zeliboba]], a 9-foot furry blue tree spirit who enjoys dancing
* [[Businka]], a bright pink Muppet who finds joy in everything
* [[Kubik]], the resident pensive problem-solver

==[[Takalani Sesame]] ([[South Africa]])==
*[[Takalani Sesame#Kami|Kami]], who raised controversy in the [[United States|USA]], due to her HIV+ status

==[[Barrio Sésamo]] ([[Spain]])==
*[[Espinete]], a large pink hedgehog
*[[Don Pimpón]]: Another full-body muppet. This farmer was an undetermined brown being, similar to a Sesame Street monster.
*[[Caponata]], a chicken equivalent to Big Bird
*[[Perezgil]], a female green snail

==[[Susam Sokaği]] ([[Turkey]])==
*[[Kirpik]], a grouch who lives in a pile of boxes
*[[Minik Kus]], a red version of Big Bird

&lt;!--This list is not international, it's characters not in the USA version--&gt;

[[Category:Lists of fictional characters|Sesame Street international characters]]
[[Category:Sesame Street characters| ]]</text>
    </revision>
