  <page>
    <title>Brachial artery</title>
    <id>231444</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38628263</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-07T16:17:11Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Arcadian</username>
        <id>104523</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>infobox / links</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Infobox Artery |
  Name        = {{PAGENAME}} |
  Latin       = A. Brachialis |
  GraySubject = 150 |
  Image       = Gray525.png |
  Caption     = The brachial artery. |
  BranchFrom  = [[axillary artery]] |
  BranchTo    = [[Profunda brachii]]&lt;BR&gt;[[Superior ulnar collateral artery]]&lt;BR&gt;[[Inferior ulnar collateral artery]]&lt;BR&gt; |
  Vein        = [[brachial vein]] |
  Supplies    = [[biceps brachii muscle]], [[triceps brachii muscle]]|
  MeshName    = Brachial+Artery |
  MeshNumber  = A07.231.114.139 |
}}
[[Image:Gray526.png|thumb|230px|Right upper limb, anterior view, '''brachial artery''' and [[elbow]].]]
The '''brachial artery''' is the major [[blood vessel]] of the upper arm.

It is a continuation of the [[axillary artery]] and it originates from the lower margin of [[teres major muscle]] and continues down the arm, until it reaches the [[cubital fossa]] at the [[elbow]]. It then ends by dividing into the [[radial artery|radial]] and [[ulnar artery|ulnar]] [[artery|arteries]] which run down the [[forearm]].

The brachial artery has smaller branches along it. These supply the muscles of the upper arm, such as [[biceps brachii muscle]] and [[triceps brachii muscle]].

The [[pulse]] of the brachial artery is [[palpation|palpable]] on the anterior aspect of the [[elbow]] and, with the use of a [[stethoscope]] and [[sphygmomanometer]] (blood pressure cuff) often used to measure the [[blood pressure]].

==External link==
* [http://www.portfolio.mvm.ed.ac.uk/studentwebs/session1/group50/arm.htm Dissection]


{{Template:BloodVessels}}

[[Category:Arteries]]
[[Category:Upper limb anatomy]]

[[de:Arteria brachialis]]
[[fr:Artère brachiale]]
[[no:Arteria brachialis]]
[[pt:Artéria braquial]]</text>
