  <page>
    <title>Fink</title>
    <id>231547</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41103997</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-25T01:48:16Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Fuhghettaboutit</username>
        <id>665998</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>prefering---&gt;preferring</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{this|fink, an open-source software project|Fink (disambiguation)}}

In [[computing]], the '''Fink''' project is an effort to [[porting|port]] [[list of popular Unix programs|popular Unix programs]] to [[Mac OS X]]. Fink uses the [[Debian]] [[package management system]], [[Advanced Packaging Tool|apt]], as well as its own frontend program, &lt;code&gt;fink&lt;/code&gt; (which is implemented as a set of [[Perl module]]s). It is maintained by a large community of contributors [http://fink.sourceforge.net/people.php?phpLang=en] who donate much of their time to package management and the project's further development.

Fink is widely recommended as the simplest way for users to install and maintain their favourite [[unix]] programs on Mac OS X. It features a binary distribution for quick and easy installation, as well as a source distribution for user preferring more flexibility. In addition to [[Command line interface|command-line]] tools for handling packages, [[FinkCommander]] provides a [[Graphical user interface|GUI]].

Fink is not compliant with the [[Filesystem Hierarchy Standard]], as it stores all its data in a hierarchy rooted at its own own directory, &quot;&lt;code&gt;/sw&lt;/code&gt;&quot; by default, rather than as part of the the base system or under &quot;&lt;code&gt;/usr/local&lt;/code&gt;&quot;.

The name &quot;Fink&quot; is [[German language|German]] for [[finch]] bird, and is related to the [[Darwin (operating system)|Darwin]] operating system (that lies at the core of Mac OS X), through [[Charles Darwin]]'s study of diversity among finches.

The Fink project was started in December, [[2000]] by German hacker Christoph Pfisterer [http://chrisp.de] who goes by the handle &quot;chrisp.&quot; He left the project in November [[2001]] &quot;after learning about the unthankfulness of people the hard way.&quot; [http://sourceforge.net/mailarchive/message.php?msg_id=243622] 

== External links ==
* [http://fink.sourceforge.net Fink project homepage]
* [irc://chat.freenode.net/fink Fink IRC channel] on [[Freenode]]

[[Category:Perl software]]
[[Category:Package management systems]]

[[de:Fink (Software)]]
[[fr:Fink]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
