    <title>Oka</title>
    <id>231559</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39900264</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-16T18:03:34Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Gauss</username>
        <id>62594</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Large parts of Siberia also belong to Russia</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Oka''' may refer to:

* ([[cars]])  '''[[Oka (car)|Oka]]''' is the name of a car produced by [[Lada]] (named after the river).
* ([[food]])  '''[[Oka cheese]]''' is a semi-soft surface ripened cheese.
* ([[food]])  '''Oka''' is an alternate spelling of [[oca]], the root vegetable.
* ([[geography]])  '''[[Oka River]]''' is a river in the European part of [[Russia]].
* ([[geography]])  '''[[Oka River, Siberia|Oka River]]''' is also a river in [[Siberia]].
* ([[geography]])  '''[[Oka, Quebec|Oka]]''' is a small town in [[Quebec]], [[Canada]].  It is noted for [[Oka cheese]] and the [[Oka Crisis]] of [[1990]].
* ([[metrics]])  '''[[Oka (measure)|Oka]]''' is [[Turkey|Turkish]] measure of [[weight]] equaled to 1.28 [[kilogram]]s.
* ([[military]])  '''&amp;#332;ka''', or [[Ohka]] was a [[kamikaze]] aircraft in [[World War II]]
* ([[military]])  The '''[[R-400 Oka]]''' is a theatre ballistic missile deployed by the [[Soviet Union]].
* ([[music]]) '''[[OKA]]''' - An [[Australia]]n based band playing didgeridoo based World Music
* ([[aviation]]) The [[IATA airport code]] for '''[[Naha Airport]]'''
* ([[lifestyles]]) '''[[OKA]]''' - Otherkin Alliance.  A web based support group for Otherkin (otherkinalliance.org).
[[bg:Ока]]
[[de:Oka]]
[[fr:Oka (homonymie)]]
[[nl:Oka]]
[[pl:Oka]]
[[ru:Ока]]
{{disambig}}</text>
