      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For [[Mithridates VI of Pontus|Mithridates]]'s strongman in [[Cappadocia]], see [[Gordius of Cappadocia]]   
'''Gordius''' was the first king of [[Phrygia]] and the father of King [[Midas]]. According to legend, he was proclaimed king in response to the decree of an [[oracle]] that he happened to be the first person to ride into the town of [[Gordium]] during a particular assembly
of the people. The legend continues that he rode into the city on a wagon, to which the [[yoke]] was attached by the [[Gordian Knot]]. Both the wagon and yoke were dedicated to the god [[Zeus]].</text>
    </revision>
