      <contributor>
        <username>Allstar86</username>
        <id>49760</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Delta Airlines -&gt; Air Lines</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Dyna-Flytes''' was a brand of die-cast [[Model aircraft|model airplanes]] produced in the [[1980s]] by [[Dee Toys]] of [[California]]. The line was part of a series of ''Dyna'' die-cast  products that included toy cars, construction vehicles, bikes, etc.

Despite having a line-up that consisted in its vast majority of military airplanes and helicopters, ''Dyna-Flytes'' is often credited with being the first brand that had commercial [[Airline|airlines]] license them to produce die-cast models of them.

Among the airlines that had models released by ''Dyna-Flytes'' are: [[FedEx]], [[Delta Air Lines]], [[Eastern Airlines]], [[Pan Am]], [[TWA]], [[Braniff]] and others.
{{toy-stub}}

[[Category:Toys]]</text>
