      <contributor>
        <ip>58.8.92.11</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* External link */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''YKK Group''' is a Japanese group of manufacturing companies.  Founded in [[1934]] by [[Tadao Yoshida]] in Higashi Nihonbashi, [[Tokyo]], it was originally known as San-Es Shokai (&amp;#12469;&amp;#12531;&amp;#12456;&amp;#12473;&amp;#21830;&amp;#20250;).  It was renamed to Yoshida Kogyosho (&amp;#21513;&amp;#30000;&amp;#24037;&amp;#26989;&amp;#25152;) in [[1938]], to Yoshida Kogyo K.K. (Yoshida Kogyo Kabushiki Kaisha, &amp;#21513;&amp;#30000;&amp;#24037;&amp;#26989;&amp;#26666;&amp;#24335;&amp;#20250;&amp;#31038;) in [[1945]], and to YKK (YKK Kabushiki Kaisha, YKK&amp;#26666;&amp;#24335;&amp;#20250;&amp;#31038;) in [[1994]].  The name YKK was first registered as a [[trademark]] in [[1946]].

Today the YKK Group is most famous for making [[zipper]]s, although it also does business in other fastening products, architectural products, and industrial machinery. 

==External link==
* [http://www.ykk.com/english/index.html YKK Group homepage] (English)
* [http://jeans.pai-nai.com/zip-fasteners-01a.html The first patent for the 'Separable Fastener' the frontrunner for todays zipper] (English)
[[Category:Companies of Japan]]

[[de:Yoshida Kōgyō Kabushikigaisha]]
