  <page>
    <title>John Maurer</title>
    <id>231781</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38288197</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-05T09:32:10Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>D6</username>
        <id>75561</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>adding [[category:Living people]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''John Maurer''' (born [[July 14]], [[1964]]) played [[bass guitar]] for [[Social Distortion]] from [[1984]] to [[2004]].  He was replaced by [[Rancid]]'s [[Matt Freeman]]. He joined [[Social Distortion]] after the departure of [[Brent Liles]].

In his later career he started two bands, Foxy and Fuel, while still playing for Social Distortion.  He also started his own record company called Slip Records.

==Discography with [[Social Distortion]]==
*''[[Prison Bound]]'' (1988)
*''[[Social Distortion (album)|Self-Titled]]'' (1990)
*''[[Somewhere Between Heaven And Hell]]'' (1992)	
*''[[White Light, White Heat, White Trash]]'' (1996)
*''[[Live at the Roxy (Social Distortion album)|Live at the Roxy]]'' (1998)

{{bassist-stub}}

[[Category:1964 births|Maurer, John]]
[[Category:Living people|Maurer, John]]
[[Category:Bassists|Maurer, John]]</text>
