'''''Mary Star of the Sea''''' is [[Zwan]]'s only album, released on [[January 28]], [[2003]].  It is a generally upbeat pop-rock record, driven by melodic basslines, flashy drumming, and lots and lots of guitars.  &quot;Honestly&quot; and &quot;Lyric&quot; were released as singles.  The album is named after a Catholic church in Key West, Florida.  Although it reached # 3 in the US, it didn't have staying power in the charts.  This likely contributed to Billy Corgan's dissolution of the band later in 2003.

