      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''Christ: The Bootleg''''' is a live album by [[Crass]], released in [[1989]]. Although a [[Bootleg recording|bootleg]], it was released in [[1997]] by [[Allied Recordings]] with the permission of the band, and then reissued by [[No Idea Records]] after Allied closed its doors. The album features cover artwork by [[anarchist]] [[artist]] [[John Yates]].

Recorded live in [[Nottingham]] [[1984]].

==Track listing==
#&quot;The Falklands (Introduction)&quot;
#&quot;Yes Sir, I Will&quot;
#&quot;Nineteen Eighty Bore&quot;
#&quot;Don't Get Caught&quot;
#&quot;The Mother Earth&quot;
#&quot;The Mother Love&quot;
#&quot;Smash The Mac&quot;
#&quot;Bata Motel&quot;
#&quot;Darling&quot;
#&quot;Poison In A Pretty Pill&quot;
#&quot;Gotcha&quot;
#&quot;Big A Little a&quot;
#&quot;Yes Sir, I Will&quot;
#&quot;Major General Despair&quot;
#&quot;Take It As Entertainment&quot;
#&quot;You're Already Dead&quot;

